    "rulesNotes": [
        "This is a fan-made 'Grade 2a' warband from The New Mordheimer (mordheimer.net), not part of the official Games Workshop core rulebook - treat it as a community supplement.",
        "A Halfling warband must include a minimum of 3 models and may contain a maximum of 20.",
        "The warband must include exactly one Halfling Elder.",
        "The warband may include a single Halfling Cook and a single Halfling Thief.",
        "The warband may include up to two Halfling Youths.",
        "The warband may include up to seven Halfling Scouts, five Halfling Warriors, and four Piggies.",
        "The warband may include a single Village Ogre.",
        "Halfling Warriors may not take a Bow. Only the Elder and Scouts may buy Hunting Arrows. Only Heroes and Warriors may take a Double-handed weapon or Spear - Scouts may not. These per-type restrictions are why this warband uses more separate equipment lists than most others in this app.",
        "The source page flavour-names some of the Halfling Cook's weapons and armour (Pairing Knife for Dagger, Tenderiser for Hammer, Meat Cleaver for Axe, Machete for Sword, Cooking Pot for Helmet) - these are the same items mechanically, just renamed for a Cook, so this app lists them under their standard names.",
        "Piggies are animals and never gain experience.",
        "This warband's own Special skills (Quiet as a Mouse, Crude Belch, Wizened Halfling, Stealthy, Skilled Huntsman, Layers of Fat, Shifty) are added to the Special category in skills.json - note Wizened Halfling is leader-only and Stealthy is Thief-only per the source text, which this app does not enforce automatically.",
        "Skill-category access for this warband's Heroes is taken directly from the source page's own skill table (its checkmarks were legible, unlike most core-rulebook warbands in this app, which needed a judgement call)."
    ]
}
